  "description": "Statelessness, which for a pseudo-conversational program means the conversation state travels in the payload and nowhere else. Everything COADM01C knows between keystrokes is CARDDEMO-COMMAREA, the attention identifier and the screen's own field values, and all three arrive in the request and leave in the response - which is the only reason the navigation expectation below is comparable at all. This case drives the same invocation three times: twice against one service instance and once against a freshly constructed one, and asserts all three outcomes are equal. A translation holding WS-ERR-FLG, WS-MESSAGE or WS-OPTION in a field of a singleton bean would leak the first call into the second and fail that, which is why those are method-local in the translation. Only the first run is reported: one invocation produces one response.",
